<section id="for-business">
  <h2>Can I build this for your business?</h2>
  <p class="lede">Most teams have someone pulling numbers into a spreadsheet every week to make the same report. I automate that, so the report builds itself and is always up to date.</p>
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="card tint-4 reveal">
      <h3>The problem</h3>
      <p class="muted">Reports made by hand take hours, arrive late, and break when someone is off sick or a spreadsheet changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card tint-1 reveal">
      <h3>What I build</h3>
      <p class="muted">A live dashboard that collects your data on a schedule, checks it, charts it and publishes it, with no one pressing a button.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card tint-3 reveal">
      <h3>The proof</h3>
      <p class="muted">This site. It gathers real news data every morning and rebuilds itself, and if a source fails it keeps the last good data. <a href="/#dashboards">See the dashboards</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h3 style="margin-top:24px">How it works</h3>
  <ol class="steps colourful">
    <li><b>Tell me about your data</b>Where it lives (spreadsheet, database, an app's API) and who needs to see it.</li>
    <li><b>I sketch the dashboard</b>The handful of numbers and charts that answer your real questions.</li>
    <li><b>I automate it</b>Data is collected and checked on a schedule, so it's always current.</li>
    <li><b>You just open a link</b>Low running cost, often free, and nothing to update by hand.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="callout">Good fits: weekly sales or stock reports, support ticket trends, campaign results, or test and release health for software teams.</p>
